#import "../design.typ": *

#chapter(number: 8, title: "A Scene Through Every Check")

Read separately, these intelligences are seven tools. Used together, on one scene,
they are a single sense — the feeling of *knowing your book* that no writer has
unaided. Let us take one chapter through all of them, in the order you would actually
reach for them, and watch the book come into focus.

The scene: chapter seven, in which Mara confronts Sella about the betrayal.

#section("First, is it true to the world?")

Before anything else, the facts. `Ctrl+B Shift+X` checks the page against the Facts
book and the compiled world.

#screen(caption: "1 · fact-check")[```
Fact-check · ch. 7
  ⚠ "she rode from Rillmark that morning" — the bible puts Rillmark
    six days away. Fix the geography or the timing.
```]

#section("Then, does the continuity hold?")

`Ctrl+B Shift+I` — the continuity ledger. Physical and temporal first.

#screen(caption: "2 · continuity (SENTINEL)")[```
  ⊗ co_location  Mara is at Rillmark and the capital in one scene (ch. 7)
```]

#section("Could she know what she confronts Sella with?")

The question continuity cannot ask. `Ctrl+B Shift+Z` — KEN.

#screen(caption: "3 · knowledge (KEN)")[```
  ⊗ premature_knowledge  Mara speaks of "the betrayal" in ch. 7 —
                         she is not told of it until ch. 9
```]

There it is — the invisible break. Mara accuses Sella of a thing she has not learned.
Move the reveal earlier, or give Mara a grant, and the scene holds.

#section("Do they sound like two people, and how does it read?")

`Ctrl+B J → Y` — the voices. And the whole book's shape, `Ctrl+B Shift+A`.

#screen(caption: "4 · voice (CHORUS) + read-through (LECTOR)")[```
  ⚠ Mara ↔ Sella (0.29) — the confrontation reads in one voice.
  ● [attention_dip] ch. 7 runs low-energy after a flat ch. 6.
```]

#section("Act on it — and confirm it landed")

Every finding above rides one worklist, `Ctrl+V Shift+R`, where each gets the right
kind of help: a rewrite you review as a diff, a decision you make ("move the reveal or
cut the line?"), a brief where structure is yours to move. Fix the scene there — and
then, before the next pass, mark a milestone and let CHRONICLE tell you the truth:

#screen(caption: "5 · did it get better? (CHRONICLE)")[```
Chronicle — since "before ch.7 pass" → now
  ✓ 3 cleared  (co_location, premature_knowledge, the voice flag)
  ▲ 0 introduced
```]

Three real problems, invisible an hour ago, found and cleared with nothing broken in
their place. That is what it means to know your book — not to hold it all in your head,
which no one can, but to have an instrument for every question you would otherwise have
to answer from memory, and the honesty to tell you when the answer changed.

#recap((
  [The intelligences compose: facts → continuity → knowledge → voice → shape → act →
  measure, on one scene.],
  [Everything converges on the `Ctrl+V Shift+R` worklist to act, and `Ctrl+B Shift+U`
  (CHRONICLE) to confirm the fix landed without collateral damage.],
  [Knowing your book is not holding it in your head — it is having an instrument for
  every question, and the honesty of a changed answer.],
))
